{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe src/rebar/_commands cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The current sweep is pinned to `cbc02f0e591d4c6811bb1bfbd87885e62098198a`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe semantic DD command lists the exact 109 current block IDs across 18 paths. Eleven paths changed since the frozen audit; the current-parent text defines each contract and word count. The focused command uses existing test paths after 5 old tests were removed and 2 moved.\n\n- `src/rebar/_commands/__init__.py` (7 current blocks) — Preserve positional safety, secret override shape, and confirmation contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/_confirm.py` (2 current blocks) — Preserve flag extraction, end-of-options handling, and text/JSON behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py` (6 current blocks) — Preserve idempotence, foreground GC, merge-driver requirement, and compatibility stamp. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py` (25 current blocks) — Preserve append/finalize ownership, signing rules, batch equivalence, and initialization backstop. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/bridge_repair.py` (1 current blocks) — Preserve forward/reverse-index invariant and lossless repair contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/claim.py` (11 current blocks) — Preserve `None` versus empty assignee, review order, parent-first cascade, and claim-loss detection. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py` (3 current blocks) — Preserve eligibility, bounded attempts, pinned ref, and cache-credit behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_disposition.py` (14 current blocks) — Preserve disposition/completion distinction, replacement/reason rules, and signed-manifest semantics. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py` (12 current blocks) — Preserve deterministic checks, distinct replacement remedies, verifier-fault handling, and ordering. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_plan.py` (1 current blocks) — Preserve planner ownership and shared derivations. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py` (1 current blocks) — Preserve full-log reconstruction responsibility and safety contract. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_recovery.py` (2 current blocks) — Preserve intent-journal states, idempotent recovery, and rollback behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py` (2 current blocks) — Preserve operation-linked trigger and single-worker lock behavior. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` (4 current blocks) — Preserve authorship ledger, orphan exclusion, and whole-fold rollback invariants. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact.py` (8 current blocks) — Preserve fold selection, no-op push contract, and artifact-based outcome. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/composer_edit.py` (6 current blocks) — Preserve edit/tag-delta contract, parser exception, and post-commit review ordering. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/composer.py` (1 current blocks) — Preserve input contract, provenance fields, and atomic CREATE result. Consumer: none found.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py` (3 current blocks) — Preserve reported fields, shared staleness authority, and read-only behavior. Consumer: none found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792772941698626049,"uuid":"68ae3a6a-60d7-4009-9db1-7673051bcd62"}